  "stem": "Prove that the sum of the first $n$ terms of an arithmetic progression with first term $a$ and common difference $d$ is $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}\\{2a + (n - 1)d\\}$.",
  "answerSpec": {
   "markScheme": {
    "points": [
     {
      "id": "p1",
      "description": "M1 writes $S_n = a + (a + d) + \\cdots + (a + (n - 1)d)$ and the same sum in reverse order.",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p2",
      "description": "M1 adds the two lines term by term: each of the $n$ pairs sums to $2a + (n - 1)d$.",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p3",
      "description": "A1 $2S_n = n\\{2a + (n - 1)d\\}$, so $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}\\{2a + (n - 1)d\\}$.",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "modelAnswer": "$$\nS_n = a + (a + d) + \\cdots + [a + (n - 2)d] + [a + (n - 1)d]\n$$\n\n$$\nS_n = [a + (n - 1)d] + [a + (n - 2)d] + \\cdots + (a + d) + a\n$$\n\nAdding, each of the $n$ columns sums to $2a + (n - 1)d$:\n\n$$\n2S_n = n\\{2a + (n - 1)d\\} \\Rightarrow S_n = \\frac{n}{2}\\{2a + (n - 1)d\\}\n$$"
  },
